<section id="west-stamford-fence" class="cs-case" aria-labelledby="case-title"><div class="cs-container"><div class="cs-editorial"><div><p class="cs-eyebrow">Featured Project / West Stamford Fence</p><h2 id="case-title">More Than a Website. A Digital System Built Around the Business.</h2></div><div><p>West Stamford Fence needed more than a polished online presence. The opportunity was to create a website that could showcase real fence installations, explain the company&#39;s services, serve customers across its Connecticut service area, and make it easier to keep the site growing with new project content.</p>
<p>Mantis Digital Media designed and developed a modern contractor website supported by a custom content management system and a mobile-friendly Project Creator.</p>
<p>The result is a connected approach to presenting the business online: a customer-facing website, project galleries, service and location content, inquiry tools, and a private system for preparing and publishing new work.</p><a class="cs-link" href="https://weststamfordfence.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Visit West Stamford Fence <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><ul class="cs-capabilities"><li>Custom responsive website</li><li>Mobile Project Creator</li><li>Private content management</li><li>AI-assisted project writing</li><li>Search-focused service and location content</li><li>Customer inquiry experience</li></ul><div class="cs-case-visual">{{ screen('wsf-homepage.png', homepageAlt, 'The West Stamford Fence homepage: the public face of the connected system.') }}</div></div></section>
<section aria-labelledby="responsive-title"><div class="cs-container"><div class="cs-section-intro"><p class="cs-eyebrow">Built for Every Screen</p><h2 id="responsive-title">A Professional First Impression, Wherever Customers Find You.</h2><p>A contractor&#39;s website needs to work just as well for someone researching services at their desk as it does for someone looking for help on their phone.</p>
<p>For West Stamford Fence, we built a responsive experience with clear service navigation, project photography, prominent estimate and contact options, and layouts designed for desktop and mobile visitors.</p></div><div class="cs-responsive-showcase">{{ screen('wsf-homepage.png', homepageAlt, 'The responsive desktop website.') }}{{ phone('wsf-mobile.png', 360, 737, 'West Stamford Fence mobile homepage with navigation and stacked estimate and contact options', 'The same website, designed for a smaller screen.') }}</div></div></section>
<section class="cs-creator" aria-labelledby="creator-title"><div class="cs-container"><div class="cs-section-intro"><p class="cs-eyebrow">The Project Creator</p><h2 id="creator-title">Your Best Work Shouldn't Stay Hidden on Your Phone.</h2><p>Every finished job is another opportunity to show prospective customers what your company can do.</p>
<p>For West Stamford Fence, Mantis built a mobile-friendly Project Creator that lets an authorized user document a completed installation and prepare it for publication on the website.</p>
<p>Instead of needing to work directly in website code, the contractor can enter project information, choose the location and fence type, add a description, and select photographs from a phone.</p>
<p>The system also supports English and Spanish speech input and AI-assisted content preparation, helping turn everyday project details into more polished website content.</p></div><div class="cs-creator-grid"><div class="cs-phone-pair">{{ phone('wsf-project-creator-1.jpg', 1080, 2400, 'Mobile Project Creator showing project information, location, fence type, description, and Save Project controls', '01 / Capture the project details.') }}{{ phone('wsf-project-creator-2.jpg', 1080, 2400, 'Mobile Project Creator showing English and Spanish speech input, Take Photos and Choose Photos controls, and No photos staged yet', '02 / Speech input and photo-selection controls.') }}</div><dl class="cs-feature-list">
<div><dt>Capture the Details</dt><dd>Enter the project name, town, fence type, and description.</dd></div>
<div><dt>Add Job Photos</dt><dd>Take photographs or choose existing images from the phone.</dd></div>
<div><dt>Speak Instead of Type</dt><dd>Use supported English or Spanish speech input to help describe the work.</dd></div>
<div><dt>Prepare the Content</dt><dd>Use AI-assisted writing to help turn project notes into readable, search-focused descriptions.</dd></div>
<div><dt>Review Before Publishing</dt><dd>Keep content within the authorized project management and publishing workflow.</dd></div>
</dl></div></div></section>
<section aria-labelledby="publishing-title"><div class="cs-container"><div class="cs-editorial"><div><p class="cs-eyebrow">From the Field to the Website</p><h2 id="publishing-title">Turn Completed Projects Into Content Customers Can Explore.</h2></div><div><p>A completed installation shouldn&#39;t disappear into a camera roll.</p>
